{
  "abstract": "In a finite binary register-machine model, if every polynomial-time word function computed using one nonadaptive batch of NP queries is computable using logarithmically many adaptive NP queries, then P equals NP. The two oracle function classes therefore coincide exactly when P equals NP. The checked algorithm recovers the affine hull of verifier witnesses by a parallel query batch, enumerates the candidates from hypothetical adaptive answer tapes, and uses either a tested witness or a parity cut to decide the instance in polynomial time.",
